# The trust root of the copy-truth checks (decision 0114): every file, and every .cairn.yml job, that decides how a pull
# request is judged. scripts/check-copy-vs-marketplace.py --mode trust-root hashes each entry into
# config/trust-root.sha256. Two checks compare them and name every entry that differs:
#   - copy-truth runs the BASE's checker with the BASE's list and manifest against the PR's tree. A PR cannot change
#     that comparison. It detects; while copy-truth is advisory it does not block (stigready-web#96 makes such a
#     change need the owner's signature).
#   - CINC web-copy-truth-08, in validate, runs the PR's own checker and manifest: a tripwire that a PR can rewrite.
# Entries: a file, a directory/** (every file under it; a symlink is refused), .cairn.yml#<job>, .cairn.yml#<job>/<step>
# or .cairn.yml#triggers/<key>. This file is always an entry itself.
scripts/check-copy-vs-marketplace.py
scripts/render/**
cinc/profiles/stigready-web/controls/copy_truth.rb
cinc/profiles/stigready-web/files/copy-truth/**
config/snapshot-signers
.cairn.yml#copy-truth
.cairn.yml#copy-drift-watch
.cairn.yml#validate/render-setup
.cairn.yml#validate/cinc-stigready-web
.cairn.yml#triggers/schedule
